  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Chairs, score folders, and the conductor’s stand need a short setup before singing; volunteers can arrive early without changing the rehearsal itself.\", \"decision\": \"How should room setup duties be shared?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers claim specific setup duties on the attendance sheet before each rehearsal, and the organizer fills any remaining gaps. Members choose tasks that fit their arrival plans while the organizer can see whether the room preparation is covered.\nAn early-arriving setup coordinator divides the listed duties among available volunteers when they reach the room. The work follows the people actually present, allowing small changes in arrival time without leaving individual tasks unassigned.\nThe organizer assigns setup duties through a rotating volunteer list and sends reminders before each rehearsal. Responsibility moves among willing members, and each person knows in advance which part of the room to prepare."
    }
  ],
